            {
              "id": "55453ad4-f45b-3aed-a0c8-b04ad2510d9e",
              "name": "resources.rules.avoid-pyyaml-load",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Opengrep Finding: resources.rules.avoid-pyyaml-load"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Avoid using `load()`. `PyYAML.load` can create arbitrary Python\nobjects. A malicious actor could exploit this to run arbitrary\ncode. Use `safe_load()` instead.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Avoid using `load()`. `PyYAML.load` can create arbitrary Python\nobjects. A malicious actor could exploit this to run arbitrary\ncode. Use `safe_load()` instead.\n\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro",
                "markdown": "Avoid using `load()`. `PyYAML.load` can create arbitrary Python\nobjects. A malicious actor could exploit this to run arbitrary\ncode. Use `safe_load()` instead.\n\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://github.com/yaml/pyyaml/wiki/PyYAML-yaml.load(input)-Deprecation](https://github.com/yaml/pyyaml/wiki/PyYAML-yaml.load(input)-Deprecation)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-18342](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-18342)\n"
